I.K.E. Windows engine: Vivaldi's platform_media, Windows video part

Software H.264 through the decoder that is part of Windows
(CLSID_CMSH264DecoderMFT in msmpeg2vdec.dll), as a media::VideoDecoder in the
renderer, with the decoder libraries loaded before the sandbox closes.

Source: Vivaldi 7.6.3797 (Chromium 140.0.7339.136), source archive
vivaldi-source_7.6.3797.tar.xz from https://vivaldi.com/source/, read from the
Git mirror https://github.com/ric2b/Vivaldi-browser at commit
bb6a67c4a38211d36180421ee814367f8d274be4.

  Copyright (c) 2018 Vivaldi Technologies AS. All rights reserved.
  Copyright (C) 2015 Opera Software ASA.  All rights reserved.
  "This file is an original work developed by Opera Software ASA"

Licence: BSD-3-Clause. The two licence texts are part of this patch:
chromium/platform_media/OPERA_LICENSE.txt (Opera Software ASA) and
chromium/platform_media/VIVALDI_LICENSE.txt (Vivaldi Technologies).

New files: chromium/platform_media/** (seven of them byte for byte as in
Vivaldi, three with small changes marked "I.K.E.:"; the list with checksums
is in chromium/platform_media/README.ike.md).

Hooks in Chromium's files, taken from Vivaldi's tree (there under its
build-wide define USE_SYSTEM_PROPRIETARY_CODECS; here under
BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS) on Windows):
  media/base/decoder.{h,cc}                  VideoDecoderType::kVivWMFDecoder
  media/renderers/default_decoder_factory.cc VivaldiDecoderConfig::AddVideoDecoders
  content/renderer/renderer_main_platform_delegate_win.cc
                                             platform_media_init::InitForRendererProcess
Vivaldi's GN file (platform_media/source_updates.gni) needs Vivaldi's own GN;
the same sources and libraries are added in media/renderers/BUILD.gn and
media/base/BUILD.gn (Vivaldi: //base).

