@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# platform_media (Windows video part), as used by I.K.E.'s Qt WebEngine
+
+Source: Vivaldi 7.6.3797 (Chromium 140.0.7339.136), folder `platform_media/`
+of Vivaldi's source archive `vivaldi-source_7.6.3797.tar.xz`
+(<https://vivaldi.com/source/>), read from the Git mirror
+<https://github.com/ric2b/Vivaldi-browser> at commit
+`bb6a67c4a38211d36180421ee814367f8d274be4`.
+
+Licence: BSD 3-clause. `OPERA_LICENSE.txt` (© 2013 Opera Software ASA) is
+Vivaldi's `platform_media/OPERA_LICENSE.txt`; `VIVALDI_LICENSE.txt`
+(© 2015 Vivaldi Technologies) is the `LICENSE` file at the root of Vivaldi's
+source archive. The file headers say which of the two applies.
+
+Unchanged files (SHA-256 as in Vivaldi 7.6.3797):
+
+    5e7a72f1af32d833a31c656bde778e17d4d072f2fcd0c4b259c42deb9fe23dcb  decoders/win/wmf_video_decoder.cc
+    ef2ac286039b27efb9579bf90d1b54906755c16903bfbbe83911a29a16e337a9  decoders/win/wmf_video_decoder.h
+    b19424060a314cb99e58ceeb56abd6d36dee8f1e5a27ed638bd56a4d05d266b5  decoders/vivaldi_decoder_config.h
+    176e4618bd6967dec372e6c95a56ad539bd49e35b043d6013edffa8ed3ccc565  decoders/platform_logging_util.cc
+    005679a99348a5ac1cbdba659f6043572b208c3c860e9018d040e4f26fb51c35  decoders/platform_logging_util.h
+    3635047b03c96f5d42917deb833713e3b2d45e4737acc1275ac24ecd92b6fcbd  decoders/debug_buffer_logger.cc
+    ab993109b7b474e19cfe4b86c851b6079755dacccc4a833697f9e899b39a1e23  decoders/debug_buffer_logger.h
+    029782271071622943436c58edf4e6e3de26d2e3879096109b6cae8200f21f7b  OPERA_LICENSE.txt
+    bf8c708b49927881e2531dcf5e788227f501f116825bb9be7708846765c638eb  VIVALDI_LICENSE.txt   (Vivaldi: LICENSE)
+
+Changed files; every change is marked with a comment that starts `I.K.E.:`:
+
+- `sandbox/win/platform_media_init.h`, `decoders/vivaldi_decoder_config.cc`:
+  the `#error` without Vivaldi's build-wide define
+  `USE_SYSTEM_PROPRIETARY_CODECS` is left out (Qt WebEngine has no such
+  define; the files are compiled only on Windows with
+  `proprietary_codecs=true`).
+- `decoders/vivaldi_decoder_config.cc`: no `#include "base/vivaldi_switches.h"`
+  (a Vivaldi file that is not used there).
+- `sandbox/win/platform_media_init.cc`: no `CHECK_NE(handle,
+  kFailedLibraryLoad)` in builds that are not "official": a Windows without
+  the decoder libraries must get "cannot play", not a crash.
+
+Not taken from `platform_media/`: the AAC decoder inside FFmpeg
+(`ffmpeg/wmfaacdec.c` and its helpers — it needs `ffmpeg_branding="Chrome"`),
+everything for macOS and Linux, Vivaldi's GN file `source_updates.gni` (it
+needs Vivaldi's own GN; the same sources and libraries are listed in
+`media/renderers/BUILD.gn` and `media/base/BUILD.gn`), and the start-up hooks
+for the GPU and utility processes (they serve the FFmpeg AAC decoder).
